# The mod's moving parts, top to bottom. Hues: ink = Claude Code, sky = wiring, sage = logic, sand = infrastructure.
title:   A small, testable core between two thin layers
caption: Claude Code tells the mod when turns start and end. A thin wiring layer passes that on to the core, which makes every decision. The core reaches the outside world only through small wrappers, and in tests those wrappers answer from memory instead.
note:    All the logic sits in core.ts and config.ts, so tests drive the real core over stand-in infrastructure, with no mocks.

row
box  engine    Claude Code — sends events, offers the $ interface   ink
row
box  register  register.ts — thin wiring, no decisions   sky
box  tools     tools.ts — the three tools Claude can call   sky
row
box  core      core.ts — IdleCompact: timer, size check, compaction   sage
box  config    config.ts — defaults, validation, layer merge   sage
row  infra.ts · Nullables
box  clock   Clock   sand
box  store   Store   sand
box  files   Files   sand
box  ui      Ui      sand
box  host    Host    sand
row
box  real    In a session — create($): wraps Claude Code's $   ink
box  stub    In tests — createNull(): answers from memory   plum dashed
tag  ink    Claude Code — the host program and its $ interface
tag  sky    Wiring — connects events and tools to the core
tag  sage   Logic — pure decisions, fully unit-tested
tag  sand   Infrastructure — one small wrapper per outside thing

engine -> register  turn.start · turn.complete · tool.run
tools -> register  registers
register -> core  calls the core
core -> config  reads
core -> infra  reads time, files, store; compacts
infra -> real
infra -> stub  dashed
